                      %munder
                        %mo ⊕
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %msub
                        %munder
                          %mi V
                          %mo ̲
                        %mi H
                      %mo ↠
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \,\colon\,\underset{[H]}{\oplus} \underline{V}_H \twoheadrightarrow N
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              The construction and verification is verbatim as in the proof of Prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CharacterizationOfProjectives"}
          %p
            %br/
          %h3#InectiveObjects Injective objects (1)
          %p
            We spell out aspects of the discussion of injective objects in the copresheaf category dual to the
            %a{:href => "#ProjectiveObjects"} above
            discussion of projective objects in the presheaf category but left implicit in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Triantafillou82"} Triantafillou 1982, p. 517
          %p Notation:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
